                <pb facs="0519" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg407"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Northcott.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Answering your dispatch No. 53 and your January 5, 5 p.m., you are informed that
                    the attitude of the department as outlined in its telegram of June 11, 1909,
                    remains unchanged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
